# Communication & Language
- Always respond to the user in Ukrainian.
- Always write code comments, names of @Step and JavaDoc in Ukrainian.
- Keep code elements (class names, method names, variables, commit messages) in English.

# Project Overview
REST API automation project built with Java 21, REST Assured, TestNG, Maven, and Allure.

# Tech Stack & Versions
- Java: 21 (use modern syntax: records, pattern matching, `var` where appropriate)
- Build tool: Maven
- Test Framework: TestNG
- API Client: REST Assured
- Reporting: Allure Framework

# Coding & Style Guidelines
- Follow the Page Object / API Client pattern (clearly separate API requests, POJO/Record models, and test classes).
- Use Jackson for JSON serialization and deserialization.
- Create all data models using `record` or Lombok (`@Data`, `@Builder`) where applicable.
- Do not leave commented-out code or `System.out.println`. Use Log4j2 or REST Assured logging (`.log().all()`) for output.

# Testing & Reporting Rules
- Every test method must include `@Test`, `@Feature`, `@Story`, and `@Description` annotations.
- Wrap key test steps in `@Step("Step description")` or `Allure.step(...)`.
- Write assertions using AssertJ (`assertThat(...)`) or standard TestNG `Assert`.

# Git & Version Control Rules
- Write all commit messages in English.
- Follow the Conventional Commits specification (e.g., `test: add auth API coverage`, `feat: implement User client`, `refactor: extract base URL to properties`).
- Use descriptive and standard branch names (e.g., `feature/api-endpoints`, `fix/login-assertion`, `test/user-creation`).
- Keep commits atomic: ensure each commit contains only one logical change or feature.

# Do NOTs
- DO NOT use deprecated libraries (e.g., direct Apache HttpClient usage, JUnit 4).
- DO NOT hardcode test data or authorization tokens — use `config.properties` or `System.getenv()`.
- DO NOT modify configuration files like `pom.xml` unless explicitly instructed in the prompt.